## Tech Stack
- React.js (Vite, functional components + hooks)
- Framer Motion — page transitions, entrance animations, gesture-based hover states
- Three.js (via React Three Fiber + Drei) — 3D icons, hover-interactive project cards
- Particles.js (or tsParticles) — mouse-reactive background particles
- Tailwind CSS — utility styling, dark theme as default (no light mode toggle needed)
- React Router — page-level routing with animated route transitions
- EmailJS or a serverless form handler — Contact page submission (no backend required)

## Global Architecture
- Single-page-app feel: each "page" below is a route, but navigation between them uses full-page 
  AnimatePresence transitions (not hard reloads) — wipe, slide, morph, or particle-dissolve, 
  a DIFFERENT signature transition per route so each section feels distinct.
- Persistent nav (fixed sidebar or top bar) with active-route indicator; collapses to a bottom 
  tab bar or hamburger on mobile.
- Global animated gradient-blur blob background, layered behind Particles.js, both stay mounted 
  across route changes so the transition doesn't feel like a reset.
- Performance: lazy-load Three.js scenes and route bundles with React.lazy/Suspense; reduce 
  particle count and disable heavy 3D on mobile viewport widths (<768px) using a device check.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion — provide a reduced-animation fallback, don't just ignore it.

